 "sentences": [
  "I'll, of course, guide you and provide any resources you need.",
  "It's important to me that you develop good habits from the start.",
  "Always remember to include them.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you have any questions or concerns in the meantime.",
  "They certainly have their purpose, but I prefer my team to develop a keen eye for detail and a sense of ownership over their code.",
  "Relying too much on a linter can make us lazy and less mindful of our work.",
  "I want you to take pride in your code and really understand it inside out.",
  "When you write code, take the time to review it yourself first.",
  "Look for errors, inconsistencies, and areas where the code can be improved.",
  "Then, before committing the code, have a colleague review it as well.",
  "By doing this, you'll not only improve your coding skills but also your critical thinking and attention to detail."
 ],
